what: The Xenocide and the Speaker — the child who won humanity's war believing it a game, annihilating the Formics, and who spent the rest of his long life carrying the last Hive Queen's cocoon across the stars to speak the dead truly and find them a world to live again.
why: Because to defeat an enemy you must first understand him, and to understand him is to love him — and the love comes too late to stop the killing; because the only atonement for ending a people is to carry their last hope and to tell the truth of every life, friend or monster, without flinching.
